      "lineNbr": 5044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like we need to check the SVID here to know whether we can do any DP stuff, but for now, I didn\u0027t want to disturb how this state works more than necessary.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5044,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 5044,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "9919e09c38c19729aaa8aca28d4a5b1321aace5e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fed954a_328b8875",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5059,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T02:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally, I think the PE would probably hand these off to the DPM, and the DPM would in turn hand off DP stuff to the DP module. This seemed to me like a reasonable intermediate form, but I\u0027m interested in other perspectives.",
      "range": {
